# FlintTrade — ai

> LLM chat, RAG, ML signals, news sentiment, autonomous trading workflows

## Absorbs
- openalgo-mcp → MCP natural language trading (15+ tools)
- openadvisor → CatBoost ML stock recommendations
- finnews-ai → financial news AI sentiment analysis

## Dependencies

See `packages/services/ai/pyproject.toml` for declared dependencies and optional extras.

## Rules
- Read root CLAUDE.md for project-wide rules
- Use `flinttrade_core.openalgo_client` (`packages/core/core/src/flinttrade_core/openalgo_client.py`) for the optional OpenAlgo REST bridge. Live writes must obtain a `SafetyContext` through `gate_order`/`gate_broker_write` and flow through `BrokerRouter`; never call broker writes directly.
- Keep shared service logic broker-neutral; broker-specific implementations and capability differences belong in gateway adapters.
- Tests are in the `tests/` directory. Add new test files as needed.
- Update root `changelog.md` only for shipped user-visible or API changes; do not add entries for tests, behaviour-preserving refactors or in-flight design.
- Branch: follow root AGENTS.md; verify live main before opening or merging a PR.

## Additional reference
- MiroFish (github.com/666ghj/MiroFish) — swarm intelligence engine with multi-agent simulation, GraphRAG, agent memory (Zep). Reference for market crowd behavior modeling and scenario prediction.
